      "ingredients": "Ingredients\n1 slab Greater Omaha US Angus Beef Ribeye\nSalt and pepper to taste\n⅓ cup olive oil\n2 sprigs rosemary\n3 cloves garlic\n2 tbsps. butter\n2 cups onion, sliced\n2 cups arugula\n6 slices sourdough bread, toasted\n½ cup horseradish",
      "procedure": "Procedure\nPat dry Greater Omaha US Angus Beef Ribeye, and season with salt and pepper.\nSet a cast iron pan over high heat. Add ¼ cup olive oil, and sear seasoned Omaha Ribeye until nicely colored on both sides. Lower the heat to medium, then add rosemary sprigs, garlic cloves and butter. Cook for another 4-6 minutes while basting. Remove from the pan, and let rest for 8 minutes before slicing.\nSauté onions in remaining olive oil until caramelized, then season with salt and pepper. Set aside.\nThinly-slice cooked Omaha Ribeye. To assemble, spread a layer of horseradish on the sourdough bread, then top with arugula, ribeye slices and caramelized onions. Top with another slice of bread."
